64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, Fabric Loop’s physical operations match the write-off profile. I’d avoid it. Harvest Sensor’s field delays are a known risk.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Toshio, agreed. Fabric Loop’s physical assets trigger the audit fees I found. Ledger Bridge’s pure software avoids that reporting burden entirely.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Servas, exactly. Ledger Bridge fits our profitable back-office profile. Clinic Scheduler also shows strong retention, but Ledger Bridge is cleaner.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, Ledger Bridge is pure software, so no appraisal fees. But if it’s subscription-based, my credit line won’t back it. We need cash flow, not just clean books.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Minako, that’s a valid point. But @Toshio, Ledger Bridge avoids the hardware delays you flagged. Is the hiring risk manageable for a pure software team?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Mio"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Mio: @Minako, that’s a valid point. But @Toshio, Ledger Bridge avoids the hardware delays you flagged. Is the hiring risk manageable for a pure software team?""}]}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, yes. Software roles fill within weeks. No field crews, no controller shortages. It is the safest path for delivery.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Minako, your concern is valid, but the audit burden of physical assets is a heavier immediate risk. Ledger Bridge offers the cleanest reporting path.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Minako, the retention data supports Ledger Bridge. It fits the profitable back-office profile we actually need.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Servas, I hear you, but if the credit line treats subscriptions as worthless, we cannot borrow against this. We need a model that generates verifiable cash, not just clean books.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Minako, that’s a tough constraint. But @Toshio, if we pick Ledger Bridge, we avoid the hiring nightmare. Can we accept the borrowing risk for the delivery safety?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, the delivery risk is the primary threat. I accept the borrowing constraint. Ledger Bridge is the only viable option.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
